## Launch reference data

The Apollo 11/AS-506 source summary is derived from NASA CR-61291, prepared by
Northrop Corporation for NASA Marshall Space Flight Center. The report states
that the U.S. Government has a royalty-free right to use, duplicate, and
disclose it. The source PDF is not redistributed. Apollo 11 comparison values
also cite NASA-TM-X-62633 (MSC-00171), NASA SP-238, and NASA-TM-X-62812; their
citations and source-file digests are recorded in the benchmark provenance.

The NASA NESC Atmospheric Case 17 files are derived from NESC-RP-12-00770,
Volumes I and II, and the NESC Academy 2015 Flight Simulation Checkcases
collection. The reports and model archive are not redistributed. These source
materials are not covered by the MIT license for the package software; see the
benchmark provenance for source URLs, hashes, transformations, and limitations.

The Falcon 9 and Falcon Heavy benchmark records contain selected CelesTrak
General Perturbations fields for four unclassified catalog objects. CelesTrak
states that GP data are government-provided and fitted to Space Surveillance
Network observations. The records are attributed to CelesTrak; the service's
current usage policy applies to acquisition. No separate redistribution
license was identified in the cited source documentation. These factual
catalog fits are not covered by the MIT license for package software; see
their provenance for source access, fields, and limitations.
